-- title:
--   Concrete smooth sphere Reeb field and tangent variational transport
-- statement:
--   For a smooth positive sphere weight $f$, extend its explicit Reeb field by radial normalization: $R(x)=R_{\mathrm{raw}}(x/|x|)$. The extension is smooth at sphere points, tangent there and satisfies the Reeb equations for $f\alpha$. For the model weight $f(u)=\operatorname{gauge}_M(u)^{-2}$, its gauge-chart pushforward equals $X_H/\alpha(X_H)$.
--
--   The extension obeys ambient radial orthogonality near sphere points. Therefore an initially tangent solution of $v'=DR(q)v$ stays tangent:
--   $$q(0)\cdot v(0)=0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad q(t)\cdot v(t)=0.$$
--   The forward radial variational correspondence consequently needs only initial tangency. The already constructed complete sphere Flow has this concrete field as the velocity of every trajectory. This last assertion concerns time derivatives; it does not establish spatial differentiability of the Flow.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** This theorem is the conjunction of 12 individually quantified results. Each conjunct retains the exact hypotheses of its local proof; the inventory is recorded with the publication artifacts.
-- source:
--   Original auxiliary results supporting the Birkhoff global-section formalization. Reeb and radial conventions: Hryniewicz, Systems of global surfaces of section for dynamically convex Reeb flows on the 3-sphere, arXiv:1105.2077v5, equations (1)-(2), Section 2.1.1 and the radial model on p. 2, https://arxiv.org/pdf/1105.2077 . Quaternionic conventions: Joung--van Koert, arXiv:2407.19159v3, Section 2.3. Supporting calculus and arithmetic: Mathlib revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474, https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/tree/0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474/Mathlib. The auxiliary identities are original coordinate and calculus arguments; this is not a claimed formalization of the analytic prescribed-binding theorem. Local outcome documentation: notes/SMOOTH_SPHERE_REEB_VARIATION.md.

